# pattern-data-model

## Core Pattern Data Structures

### Pattern
- Unique identifier
- Quantum state vector (position, phase, amplitude)
- Coherence value (0.0-1.0) indicating pattern stability
- Generation count tracking evolutionary history
- Pattern relationships with coherence thresholds
- Memory tier assignment (STM/MTM/LTM)

### Pattern Evolution Pipeline
- Initial pattern extraction from input data
- Quantum state preparation with configurable parameters
- Coherence calculation through quantum dot product
- Stability assessment based on historical coherence
- Relationship graph maintenance with coherence thresholds
- Pattern promotion/demotion between memory tiers

### Memory Tier Management 
- Short-Term Memory (STM): Coherence >= 0.2
- Medium-Term Memory (MTM): Coherence >= 0.5
- Long-Term Memory (LTM): Coherence >= 0.8
- Promotion requires sustained coherence above threshold
- Demotion triggered by coherence drops below 0.3
- Memory pressure triggers cleanup of low coherence patterns

### Pattern Processing
- Quantum Binary State Analysis (QBSA) for pattern matching
- Quantum Fourier Hierarchy (QFH) for state transitions
- Pattern mutation based on:
  - Current coherence level
  - Relationship network topology  
  - Historical stability metrics
  - Memory tier assignments

### Pattern Relationships
- Bidirectional links between related patterns
- Coherence-based relationship strength (0.0-1.0)
- Relationship pruning below 0.3 coherence
- Automatic relationship formation above 0.7 coherence
- Graph structure maintenance for pattern evolution

### Coherence Metrics
- Base coherence from quantum state overlap
- Stability factor from historical coherence
- Generation bonus for evolved patterns
- Access frequency multiplier
- Memory tier weighting
- Relationship network density

